DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T163000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Girls Soccer at Salem (L 1–2)
LOCATION:Bertram Field\, Salem
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 1\, Salem 2\nMia St. Pi
 erre scored with eight minutes to go\, but Danvers couldn't find the equal
 izer. A long-range strike by Jackie Fritz held up as the winner\, and Sale
 m beat Danvers for the first time in close to 20 years.\nSchedule and resu
 lts: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:girls-soccer-16@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261021T183000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Girls Soccer vs Masconomet (W 3–2)
LOCATION:Dr. Deering Stadium\, Danvers
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nFinal: Danvers 3\, Masconomet 2\nOn Pi
 nk Out night\, Rylee Sullivan\, Emma Sutherland and Mia St. Pierre scored 
 and the Falcons held a 3–2 lead through the last 15 minutes to beat Masc
 onomet\, a month after losing 5–1 in Boxford. The win clinched a state t
 ournament berth for the 35th straight season and was coach Jimmy Hinchion'
 s 425th career victory.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathle
 tics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/soccer/schedule.html?team=girls
END:VEVENT
